//
// File:    std/driver_security_test.skink
// Purpose: Security regression tests for the compiler driver and
//          emitter diagnostics:
//            VULN-01 — the driver used to shell out to clang via
//              system() with raw argv interpolation; a source file or
//              -o name containing `;`, `$()`, or spaces executed shell
//              commands. The driver now execs clang via argv arrays and
//              writes the intermediate .ll into an O_EXCL temp file.
//            VULN-10 — DWARF DIFile metadata interpolated unescaped
//              directory/file names; a path containing `"` injected
//              arbitrary LLVM metadata. Paths are now escaped.
//          Runs standalone (module main); run_tests.sh exports SKINK_BIN.
// Author:  Mark Oxley
// Created: 2026
